1
00:02:41,120 --> 00:02:42,360
Want to use this to hold them together?

2
00:02:42,440 --> 00:02:43,640
Oh.

3
00:02:46,040 --> 00:02:47,840
Worst birthday ever!

4
00:02:47,920 --> 00:02:49,600
Korn, don't! Stop!

5
00:02:49,680 --> 00:02:51,440
-Listen to me first!
-Leave me alone!

6
00:02:51,520 --> 00:02:54,920
I should've hugged Dad
before he left for work.

7
00:02:56,000 --> 00:02:56,960
I'd like to order--

8
00:02:57,760 --> 00:02:58,760
Thief!

9
00:02:59,440 --> 00:03:00,480
Thief!

10
00:03:01,120 --> 00:03:03,480
-My son isn't a thief--
-Forget it, Mom.

11
00:03:03,560 --> 00:03:05,320
Let her think whatever she wants.

12
00:03:08,600 --> 00:03:10,840
<i>The doctor found a brain tumor.</i>

13
00:03:10,920 --> 00:03:12,720
What if he doesn't have surgery?

14
00:03:12,800 --> 00:03:17,560
Korn's symptoms could become more severe.

15
00:03:17,640 --> 00:03:20,400
He might not be this lucky again.

16
00:03:20,480 --> 00:03:21,320
Wait for me, please.

17
00:03:22,720 --> 00:03:23,840
Let me come with you.

18
00:03:40,640 --> 00:03:45,160
Who would've thought a tycoon's daughter
would walk around a night market?

19
00:03:52,880 --> 00:03:53,720
Hey.

20
00:03:55,480 --> 00:03:56,720
What are you looking at?

21
00:03:58,080 --> 00:03:59,120
Nothing.

22
00:03:59,720 --> 00:04:02,800
I saw you staring at that lady.

23
00:04:02,880 --> 00:04:03,960
Sorry.

24
00:04:15,120 --> 00:04:16,839
Let me come with you.

25
00:05:01,640 --> 00:05:04,080
-What are you doing, Kong?
-Wee.

26
00:05:05,800 --> 00:05:09,160
-Are you breaking into that car?
-Stay out of it.

27
00:05:09,760 --> 00:05:11,560
-Are you crazy?
-What's your problem?

28
00:05:12,160 --> 00:05:14,720
It's my business.
Can you just stay out of it?

29
00:05:15,360 --> 00:05:16,360
Hey!

30
00:05:16,440 --> 00:05:17,400
Whoa.

31
00:05:21,200 --> 00:05:22,560
What are you doing?

32
00:05:23,880 --> 00:05:25,480
It's you?

33
00:05:27,240 --> 00:05:28,400
What's going on?

34
00:05:29,280 --> 00:05:31,080
He's trying to break into your car.

35
00:05:32,040 --> 00:05:34,720
-I'm not.
-You still have the nerve to lie?

36
00:05:34,800 --> 00:05:36,480
The evidence is right in front of us.

37
00:05:37,160 --> 00:05:38,880
I was trying to stop my friend.

38
00:05:39,640 --> 00:05:43,720
Explain that to the police.
Don't you know who I am?

39
00:05:44,400 --> 00:05:45,880
You messed with the wrong person.

40
00:05:55,000 --> 00:05:57,480
Yes, Nada? How can I help you?

41
00:05:57,560 --> 00:05:59,920
<i>Could you call your brother and stop him?</i>

42
00:06:01,360 --> 00:06:02,880
What trouble did he cause this time?

43
00:06:11,840 --> 00:06:14,960
-Mrs. Walai.
-Oh, Mr. Thamrong.

44
00:06:15,040 --> 00:06:17,880
Mr. Nimit sent me.
He asked me to help with Rawee's case.

45
00:06:18,680 --> 00:06:22,800
Thank you so much. Wee would never steal.
It must be a misunderstanding.

46
00:06:22,880 --> 00:06:24,360
Of course. I'll talk to them for you.

47
00:06:24,440 --> 00:06:25,720
Thank you.

48
00:06:26,400 --> 00:06:28,040
INQUIRY ROOM

49
00:06:28,120 --> 00:06:31,680
-You should've listened to me.
-Look.

50
00:06:32,600 --> 00:06:35,080
I saw it with my own eyes.
He was breaking into your car.

51
00:06:35,920 --> 00:06:39,960
A kid like that will grow up
to be a thief if you let him go.

52
00:06:40,040 --> 00:06:42,840
If his parents can't raise him properly,

53
00:06:42,920 --> 00:06:45,600
then let him go to jail
and learn his lesson.

54
00:06:46,440 --> 00:06:47,880
I'm Rawee's mother.

55
00:06:48,480 --> 00:06:52,560
I raised my son well. He is not a bad kid.

56
00:06:52,640 --> 00:06:54,720
Please take that back.

57
00:06:55,960 --> 00:06:58,640
Not a bad kid?
Because he's such a good son,

58
00:06:59,240 --> 00:07:00,680
you two are working together, huh?

59
00:07:02,120 --> 00:07:03,400
Mr. Jak.

60
00:07:05,360 --> 00:07:07,080
You should go back for now.

61
00:07:09,960 --> 00:07:11,240
-Mr. Thamrong.
-Yes.

62
00:07:11,760 --> 00:07:14,640
Please handle this. He's still young.
I don't want this on his record.

63
00:07:14,720 --> 00:07:15,680
Of course.

64
00:07:16,720 --> 00:07:17,440
Alright.

65
00:07:17,520 --> 00:07:19,520
Ms. Da, let's go.

66
00:07:29,400 --> 00:07:30,440
It really is Ms. Da.

67
00:07:31,920 --> 00:07:34,360
Yes. That's Ms. Nada Tayawat,

68
00:07:35,040 --> 00:07:39,120
-Tayawat Group's Vice President.
-Why was she with Mr. Jak?

69
00:07:39,720 --> 00:07:42,720
She's a friend of Mr. Nimit's.
Is something wrong?

70
00:07:43,760 --> 00:07:47,280
-Oh, no. Nothing. Let's hurry inside.
-Let's go.

71
00:07:51,680 --> 00:07:52,920
Wee.

72
00:07:53,440 --> 00:07:55,960
You didn't do anything wrong.
Don't be afraid, son.

73
00:07:57,080 --> 00:08:00,320
Officer, can this matter be settled?

74
00:08:00,920 --> 00:08:02,240
He intended to steal.

75
00:08:02,320 --> 00:08:05,200
That's a criminal offense.
It can't be settled.

76
00:08:05,280 --> 00:08:06,200
Let's go.

77
00:08:06,800 --> 00:08:07,960
I'm here to turn myself in.

78
00:08:09,880 --> 00:08:12,000
Rawee tried to stop me.

79
00:08:13,400 --> 00:08:15,160
I'm the one who broke into the car.

80
00:08:20,440 --> 00:08:21,480
CRIME SUPPRESSION INSPECTOR

81
00:08:25,440 --> 00:08:28,520
Uncle, what's going to happen
to my friend?

82
00:08:29,320 --> 00:08:32,559
Rawee, you should stop
being friends with someone like him.

83
00:08:32,640 --> 00:08:35,000
He'll only bring trouble into your life.

84
00:08:38,320 --> 00:08:40,480
Wee, go wait for me in the car.

85
00:08:42,880 --> 00:08:44,400
-Thank you.
-Of course.

86
00:08:46,880 --> 00:08:47,920
Get some rest.

87
00:08:50,200 --> 00:08:52,320
Can I ask you something?

88
00:08:52,400 --> 00:08:54,680
Is Ms. Nada Mr. Rawich's wife,

89
00:08:54,760 --> 00:08:57,720
the one who was reported
to have been shot on Tawan Island?

90
00:08:58,320 --> 00:08:59,600
Yes, she's the same person.

91
00:09:00,840 --> 00:09:02,680
At the time,
I thought she wouldn't make it.

92
00:09:03,440 --> 00:09:04,560
What do you mean?

93
00:09:05,320 --> 00:09:09,560
After the attack,
Ms. Nada couldn't remember anyone.

94
00:09:09,640 --> 00:09:13,320
Mr. Nimit told me
her brain was affected by the injury.

95
00:09:13,400 --> 00:09:17,400
She's better now,
but she still can't remember many things.

96
00:09:19,200 --> 00:09:20,320
No wonder.

97
00:09:21,080 --> 00:09:22,040
No wonder what?

98
00:09:23,560 --> 00:09:26,920
-Nothing. I should get going.
-Okay.

99
00:09:30,120 --> 00:09:32,120
Thank you so much, Mr. Thamrong.

100
00:09:32,200 --> 00:09:35,720
Please thank Mr. Nimit for helping Rawee.

101
00:09:36,400 --> 00:09:38,280
Of course. I'll let him know.

102
00:09:47,080 --> 00:09:48,520
BRAIN TUMORS

103
00:09:48,600 --> 00:09:50,120
THE EARLIER YOU KNOW
THE EASIER THEY ARE TO TREAT

104
00:09:53,520 --> 00:09:55,520
BRAIN TUMORS

105
00:09:55,600 --> 00:09:57,360
A HIDDEN DANGER BEHIND CHRONIC HEADACHES

106
00:10:28,880 --> 00:10:29,720
Look at this, Wee.

107
00:10:34,600 --> 00:10:36,160
Why are you showing me this?

108
00:10:37,920 --> 00:10:41,240
Look closely at the woman.
Does she look familiar?

109
00:10:57,080 --> 00:10:59,280
This is a photo of your father and mother.

110
00:11:14,160 --> 00:11:16,840
I'm not Aunt Kan's son?

111
00:11:26,200 --> 00:11:29,200
Your father is Mr. Rawich.

112
00:11:30,800 --> 00:11:32,360
Your mother

113
00:11:33,560 --> 00:11:36,560
is Ms. Nada Tayawat.

114
00:11:38,400 --> 00:11:40,120
Wee.

115
00:11:40,960 --> 00:11:44,480
I'm sorry for lying to you all this time.

116
00:11:51,600 --> 00:11:54,240
Don't worry, Mr. Rawich and Mrs. Nada.

117
00:11:54,320 --> 00:11:56,160
Go take care of your business.

118
00:11:56,240 --> 00:11:59,200
We'll take good care of your son.

119
00:12:00,320 --> 00:12:04,440
He's still so young. I didn't want
to take him across to the island by boat.

120
00:12:04,520 --> 00:12:08,280
That's for the best.
The rough waves would be hard on him.

121
00:12:12,360 --> 00:12:16,240
Why don't you stay here tonight?
Leave tomorrow.

122
00:12:17,520 --> 00:12:19,200
It'll give him time to adjust.

123
00:12:19,840 --> 00:12:23,680
He'll probably fuss in a new place
without his mother.

124
00:12:36,600 --> 00:12:40,800
He's easy to look after.
He's already asleep. What a relief.

125
00:12:40,880 --> 00:12:44,080
It's wonderful that he has little Korn
as a playmate.

126
00:12:45,320 --> 00:12:48,520
Yes. Is his name just Rawee?

127
00:12:49,520 --> 00:12:50,680
Yes.

128
00:12:50,760 --> 00:12:54,560
What a beautiful name.
He was named after his father, wasn't he?

129
00:12:55,520 --> 00:13:00,160
Yes. Rawee and Rawich sound alike.

130
00:13:01,120 --> 00:13:02,520
How lovely.

131
00:13:17,400 --> 00:13:20,840
Not long after your parents left
for Tawan Island,

132
00:13:21,640 --> 00:13:24,880
Mr. Rawich called and told us
to take you and run.

133
00:13:24,960 --> 00:13:29,280
He told us never to return you
to the Tayawat family.

134
00:13:30,760 --> 00:13:32,040
Why?

135
00:13:37,280 --> 00:13:40,080
At first, your father and I were confused.

136
00:13:40,600 --> 00:13:42,720
But when we saw the news

137
00:13:43,560 --> 00:13:46,520
that your parents had been attacked
on Tawan Island,

138
00:13:47,920 --> 00:13:50,880
Dad decided to move us here.

139
00:13:52,000 --> 00:13:53,280
What happened to my father?

140
00:13:55,440 --> 00:13:56,720
He was shot and killed.

141
00:14:00,760 --> 00:14:04,400
As for Ms. Nada,
she was seriously injured.

142
00:14:05,800 --> 00:14:09,240
After that, I never heard from her again.

143
00:14:10,120 --> 00:14:11,920
Until I saw her at the hospital.

144
00:14:17,720 --> 00:14:20,200
I found this in the bag
with your baby belongings.

145
00:14:22,240 --> 00:14:24,000
I think this ring

146
00:14:24,600 --> 00:14:27,320
can prove to Ms. Nada

147
00:14:28,840 --> 00:14:32,480
that you really are her biological son.

148
00:14:35,600 --> 00:14:37,200
You don't love me anymore, do you?

149
00:14:40,520 --> 00:14:41,880
That's not true, Wee.

150
00:14:42,920 --> 00:14:44,840
I still love you the same.

151
00:14:45,640 --> 00:14:48,080
You will always be my son.

152
00:14:49,640 --> 00:14:52,360
Then why were you thinking
of giving me back to them?

153
00:14:52,440 --> 00:14:55,040
-Wee.
-You could've just thrown everything away.

154
00:14:56,160 --> 00:14:58,440
You didn't have to tell me.

155
00:14:58,520 --> 00:15:01,080
It would've been better
if I believed I was Aunt Kan's son.

156
00:15:02,920 --> 00:15:06,760
Why, Mom? You don't want
to raise me anymore, right?

157
00:15:08,720 --> 00:15:11,280
It was too hard, wasn't it, Mom?

158
00:15:12,200 --> 00:15:16,160
That's not true, Wee.

159
00:15:16,240 --> 00:15:18,400
Please let me explain first.

160
00:15:19,440 --> 00:15:22,240
I only just found out from Mr. Thamrong

161
00:15:22,320 --> 00:15:25,640
that Ms. Nada had lost
some of her memories.

162
00:15:26,600 --> 00:15:28,480
Part of me was relieved

163
00:15:29,400 --> 00:15:31,840
that I wouldn't
have to give you back to her.

164
00:15:34,520 --> 00:15:36,400
But if I did that,

165
00:15:37,520 --> 00:15:40,920
I would regret it for the rest of my life.

166
00:15:41,680 --> 00:15:43,240
I don't want to go, Mom.

167
00:15:44,800 --> 00:15:46,920
Please let me stay with you.

168
00:15:47,520 --> 00:15:49,040
I promise, Mom.

169
00:15:49,120 --> 00:15:51,320
I'll help you work and earn money.

170
00:15:51,400 --> 00:15:53,680
I won't be difficult.

171
00:15:53,760 --> 00:15:57,840
I won't eat too much.
Please let me stay with you.

172
00:15:58,520 --> 00:15:59,400
Wee.

173
00:15:59,480 --> 00:16:01,680
Let me stay with my brother, Mom.

174
00:16:03,320 --> 00:16:05,240
But your real mother

175
00:16:05,320 --> 00:16:08,760
has both money and power
to help you move forward.

176
00:16:11,320 --> 00:16:15,080
I don't want you
to lose your opportunities.

177
00:16:16,400 --> 00:16:18,600
I don't want anything, Mom.

178
00:16:20,880 --> 00:16:22,920
All I want is you, Mom,

179
00:16:24,080 --> 00:16:26,760
and my brother, Phakorn.
That's all I need.

180
00:16:28,160 --> 00:16:30,480
But I don't want to take advantage of you.

181
00:16:31,440 --> 00:16:34,000
Especially with your brother being sick,

182
00:16:34,720 --> 00:16:37,960
I have to give everything I have
to take care of him.

183
00:16:40,560 --> 00:16:43,280
That wouldn't be fair to you, my son.

184
00:16:51,560 --> 00:16:53,880
If you go live with them,

185
00:16:55,880 --> 00:16:58,360
I won't have to worry about you anymore.

186
00:17:00,000 --> 00:17:04,079
What if Ms. Nada doesn't remember
and refuses to accept me?

187
00:17:06,839 --> 00:17:09,000
No matter how it turns out,

188
00:17:11,640 --> 00:17:14,200
you are our family.

189
00:17:15,960 --> 00:17:18,560
You are my son.

190
00:17:21,000 --> 00:17:22,079
This house

191
00:17:22,160 --> 00:17:24,960
will always welcome you, my son.

192
00:18:46,040 --> 00:18:47,800
If you go live with them,

193
00:18:48,400 --> 00:18:50,880
I won't have to worry about you anymore.

194
00:18:50,960 --> 00:18:53,240
What if Ms. Nada doesn't remember

195
00:18:53,800 --> 00:18:55,280
and refuses to accept me?

196
00:18:55,800 --> 00:18:57,960
No matter how it turns out,

197
00:18:58,040 --> 00:19:00,880
you are our family.

198
00:19:00,960 --> 00:19:04,200
You are my son.

199
00:19:06,200 --> 00:19:09,680
<i>This house will always</i>
<i>welcome you, my son.</i>

200
00:19:17,600 --> 00:19:18,800
Nada Tayawat.

201
00:19:33,920 --> 00:19:35,120
BRAIN TUMORS

202
00:19:35,200 --> 00:19:36,200
THE EARLIER YOU KNOW
THE EASIER THEY ARE TO TREAT

203
00:19:36,280 --> 00:19:37,960
Brain tumor.

204
00:19:48,000 --> 00:19:49,800
Am I going to die, Wee?

205
00:19:55,000 --> 00:19:56,720
Why would you say that?

206
00:19:57,840 --> 00:20:01,000
You're still so young.
Why are you talking about dying?

207
00:20:03,960 --> 00:20:06,240
I have a brain tumor, right?

208
00:20:11,120 --> 00:20:15,200
I looked it up,
and all the symptoms match.

209
00:20:17,360 --> 00:20:19,240
The doctors are looking for a treatment.

210
00:20:20,080 --> 00:20:22,760
Don't be afraid, Korn.
You're going to get better.

211
00:20:24,480 --> 00:20:27,520
-But what if--
-Don't think that far ahead, Korn.

212
00:20:29,120 --> 00:20:31,240
The doctor said there's a way to treat it.

213
00:20:31,840 --> 00:20:34,040
A lot of people have recovered from this.

214
00:20:34,920 --> 00:20:36,640
Trust me, Korn.

215
00:20:37,800 --> 00:20:39,480
You're going to get better.

216
00:20:40,320 --> 00:20:43,320
All you need is the strength to fight it.

217
00:20:48,520 --> 00:20:52,160
Can you not tell Mom that I know?

218
00:20:53,720 --> 00:20:56,840
She already has so much to worry about.

219
00:20:57,680 --> 00:21:00,000
I want things to be like they were.

220
00:21:01,840 --> 00:21:03,880
I don't want to see Mom sad.

221
00:21:08,680 --> 00:21:10,720
This will be our secret.

222
00:21:14,840 --> 00:21:16,600
Get some rest, Korn.

223
00:21:17,400 --> 00:21:19,360
Tomorrow, we'll go home together.

224
00:21:28,720 --> 00:21:31,080
I wish Dad were here.

225
00:21:38,680 --> 00:21:40,120
I'm here with you.

226
00:21:41,360 --> 00:21:42,680
Don't be afraid.

227
00:22:19,000 --> 00:22:20,280
Good morning.

228
00:22:20,360 --> 00:22:23,040
-Oh, you two came at the perfect time.
-Good morning.

229
00:22:25,920 --> 00:22:28,480
We're having guests for dinner tonight.

230
00:22:28,560 --> 00:22:29,400
Who?

231
00:22:30,000 --> 00:22:32,560
Mrs. Walai and her son,
the ones who saved me.

232
00:22:33,760 --> 00:22:35,600
Why invite them over?

233
00:22:35,680 --> 00:22:38,600
Just give them
a little money as a gesture.

234
00:22:38,680 --> 00:22:40,560
There's no need
to have them come for dinner.

235
00:22:41,680 --> 00:22:43,440
They wouldn't accept money.

236
00:22:43,520 --> 00:22:47,280
They'd see it as an insult.
I know this family well.

237
00:22:49,840 --> 00:22:53,800
You want me and Aunt Pat
to have dinner with them too, right?

238
00:22:55,080 --> 00:22:57,280
Consider it our family's way
of saying thank you.

239
00:22:59,440 --> 00:23:00,440
Okay.

240
00:23:02,520 --> 00:23:05,000
If we're back in time.

241
00:23:05,080 --> 00:23:07,760
I was actually planning to take Alyssa

242
00:23:07,840 --> 00:23:10,760
to meet some relatives.

243
00:23:13,040 --> 00:23:14,800
We haven't seen them in a long time.

244
00:23:17,360 --> 00:23:18,200
Alright.

245
00:23:18,720 --> 00:23:20,400
I'll take that as your promise, then.

246
00:23:20,480 --> 00:23:24,160
Yes. I'll try to be back in time.

247
00:23:26,160 --> 00:23:27,160
I'm going to work now.

248
00:23:40,480 --> 00:23:42,360
Hey, Alyssa.

249
00:23:42,440 --> 00:23:46,320
Be careful that your father
doesn't fall into that widow's trap.

250
00:23:46,400 --> 00:23:49,120
Her husband died,
so she's probably looking for someone new.

251
00:23:50,880 --> 00:23:54,440
You can't stop people
from falling in love. I think

252
00:23:54,960 --> 00:23:56,400
you know that better than anyone.

253
00:23:57,080 --> 00:23:58,240
Alyssa.

254
00:24:19,160 --> 00:24:20,800
Mom!

255
00:24:22,040 --> 00:24:25,200
-I've figured it out.
-What is it, son?

256
00:24:25,720 --> 00:24:29,480
What if you tell Ms. Nada
that Korn is her son?

257
00:24:33,200 --> 00:24:36,120
Mom, Korn could get surgery
from a doctor in Bangkok.

258
00:24:36,200 --> 00:24:38,480
We wouldn't have to worry about the cost.

259
00:24:39,160 --> 00:24:41,840
Korn would get the best treatment.

260
00:24:42,520 --> 00:24:43,520
That's a crazy idea.

261
00:24:44,840 --> 00:24:46,640
It's not crazy, Mom.

262
00:24:46,720 --> 00:24:49,160
Only you know the truth about this.

263
00:24:49,240 --> 00:24:52,160
If we use the diary
and that ring as proof,

264
00:24:52,760 --> 00:24:54,600
I'm sure she'll remember.

265
00:25:00,440 --> 00:25:02,440
Stop talking nonsense, Wee.

266
00:25:02,520 --> 00:25:04,920
I'll pretend we never
had this conversation.

267
00:25:05,520 --> 00:25:08,000
Don't ever bring this up again.
Do you understand?

268
00:25:10,080 --> 00:25:13,680
Wee! Did you buy meatballs for me?

269
00:25:14,520 --> 00:25:16,760
Here. I bought the whole shop.

270
00:25:17,360 --> 00:25:19,080
Whoa, awesome.

271
00:25:21,400 --> 00:25:23,160
-Let me see.
-Here you go.

272
00:25:23,240 --> 00:25:24,600
-How many sticks are there?
-Here.

273
00:25:30,400 --> 00:25:31,960
Hello, Mr. Jak.

274
00:25:34,680 --> 00:25:35,720
Sit down.

275
00:25:40,720 --> 00:25:42,080
What did you find out?

276
00:25:47,440 --> 00:25:50,200
The shares Mr. Nimit forced you to sell

277
00:25:50,280 --> 00:25:53,280
were left to Ms. Alyssa in his will.

278
00:25:59,600 --> 00:26:01,000
What the hell?

279
00:26:01,080 --> 00:26:04,400
He gave everything to his daughter,
even the land.

280
00:26:07,320 --> 00:26:11,400
But you still hold an important position
at the factory, Mr. Jak.

281
00:26:16,640 --> 00:26:18,000
If it weren't for that girl…

282
00:26:18,640 --> 00:26:19,920
What did you say, Mr. Jak?

283
00:26:21,040 --> 00:26:23,040
Nothing. You can go now.

284
00:26:38,160 --> 00:26:39,000
Oh.

285
00:26:39,080 --> 00:26:41,440
Why are you all dressed up, dear?

286
00:26:42,600 --> 00:26:43,520
Well…

287
00:26:44,480 --> 00:26:48,840
Even if I don't eat,
I should greet the guests. For Dad's sake.

288
00:26:49,840 --> 00:26:53,520
Alyssa, you always think I'm gossiping.

289
00:26:53,600 --> 00:26:58,000
But honestly, that mother and son
can't be trusted.

290
00:26:58,080 --> 00:27:01,680
They steal phones,
then pretend to be good citizens.

291
00:27:01,760 --> 00:27:03,840
Who knows if they're scammers?

292
00:27:03,920 --> 00:27:06,760
I think it's best

293
00:27:06,840 --> 00:27:09,440
we don't associate with them anymore.

294
00:27:11,280 --> 00:27:13,120
But I already promised Dad.

295
00:27:14,360 --> 00:27:17,960
If you really don't want to go down,

296
00:27:18,040 --> 00:27:21,720
just tell me. I'll take care of it.

297
00:27:27,800 --> 00:27:30,120
Wee!

298
00:27:33,960 --> 00:27:35,080
Here.

299
00:27:35,800 --> 00:27:36,960
What is it?

300
00:27:37,040 --> 00:27:40,640
Hey, if you're going to dinner,
you should dress up a little.

301
00:27:41,320 --> 00:27:43,000
It's just dinner.

302
00:27:44,040 --> 00:27:47,600
But I heard the daughter
of that family is pretty too.

303
00:27:47,680 --> 00:27:50,240
Maybe she'll fall for my big brother.

304
00:27:51,520 --> 00:27:54,400
A spoiled rich girl
with an attitude like that? No way.

305
00:27:56,000 --> 00:27:58,400
But she's from Bangkok too.

306
00:27:58,920 --> 00:27:59,960
I want to see her.

307
00:28:00,840 --> 00:28:04,600
She's nothing special.
People just exaggerate.

308
00:28:04,680 --> 00:28:07,000
Hey, why are you smiling?

309
00:28:07,640 --> 00:28:08,560
I'm not.

310
00:28:08,640 --> 00:28:10,400
Come on.

311
00:28:10,480 --> 00:28:12,360
You're acting strange.

312
00:28:13,440 --> 00:28:15,960
This outfit, right? Fine.

313
00:28:17,120 --> 00:28:18,080
Huh?

314
00:28:24,240 --> 00:28:27,280
Wee, it has to be folded like this.

315
00:28:27,360 --> 00:28:29,840
That's what makes it look cool.
This is too plain.

316
00:28:29,920 --> 00:28:31,680
How much difference does it make?

317
00:28:35,120 --> 00:28:37,680
Wow!

318
00:28:37,760 --> 00:28:38,880
Oh, you two!

319
00:28:38,960 --> 00:28:40,760
What am I going to do with you?

320
00:28:40,840 --> 00:28:44,080
Mom, you should dress like this every day.
You look amazing.

321
00:28:44,680 --> 00:28:47,960
Where would I dress like this?
I sell curry and rice every day.

322
00:28:48,040 --> 00:28:51,080
Dress like this to sell curry and rice.
The prettiest vendor around.

323
00:28:51,160 --> 00:28:52,920
Oh, you!

324
00:28:54,000 --> 00:28:55,720
Korn, you'll be okay by yourself, right?

325
00:28:55,800 --> 00:28:58,280
If anything happens, call me.
I'll come back right away.

326
00:28:59,760 --> 00:29:03,520
I'll be fine, madam.
I'll retire to my room once you leave.

327
00:29:04,760 --> 00:29:05,720
Very good.

328
00:29:06,840 --> 00:29:09,280
-Come on, Wee. We can't be late.
-Yes. Let's go.

329
00:29:09,360 --> 00:29:10,880
-Good luck.
-We'll be back. Let's go.

330
00:29:15,000 --> 00:29:16,840
JAK

331
00:29:22,040 --> 00:29:23,000
What is it?

332
00:29:23,760 --> 00:29:25,040
Are you home?

333
00:29:26,240 --> 00:29:27,920
I need to talk to you right now.

334
00:29:28,560 --> 00:29:31,840
I'm busy today. I have guests.
We'll talk tomorrow.

335
00:29:33,600 --> 00:29:37,320
Wait. Hello?

336
00:29:45,280 --> 00:29:48,800
Anyone would have helped.
It's just the right thing to do.

337
00:29:49,520 --> 00:29:52,040
We're happy that you are safe.

338
00:29:52,560 --> 00:29:55,760
Talking with you reminds me of Kiat.

339
00:29:56,520 --> 00:29:58,760
No wonder you two are husband and wife.

340
00:30:00,440 --> 00:30:02,480
I heard from Thamrong
that you've joined a club.

341
00:30:03,480 --> 00:30:06,640
-Yes, sir.
-That's great. I'm happy for you.

342
00:30:08,120 --> 00:30:09,560
Thank you.

343
00:30:10,440 --> 00:30:13,520
Soon your mother
won't have to work so hard anymore.

344
00:30:13,600 --> 00:30:16,040
Take Thai football
all the way to the World Cup.

345
00:30:16,640 --> 00:30:17,800
Of course.

346
00:30:18,720 --> 00:30:20,560
You're not modest at all.

347
00:30:24,000 --> 00:30:27,720
Why hasn't Alyssa come down yet?
She has no sense of timing.

348
00:30:34,360 --> 00:30:36,440
Alyssa won't be joining us for dinner.

349
00:30:37,160 --> 00:30:38,480
Oh? Why not?

350
00:30:39,640 --> 00:30:41,880
She said she has a headache.

351
00:30:41,960 --> 00:30:45,400
She seemed fine just now.
I'll go get her myself.

352
00:30:45,480 --> 00:30:46,680
It's okay.

353
00:30:46,760 --> 00:30:48,600
No, I can't let this go.

354
00:30:48,680 --> 00:30:51,160
I need to teach my daughter
to keep her promises.

355
00:31:11,640 --> 00:31:12,480
Hey.

356
00:31:14,320 --> 00:31:16,760
You know, you could've just refused.

357
00:31:17,680 --> 00:31:20,320
Who would want to have dinner
with strangers?

358
00:31:21,960 --> 00:31:23,560
How could anyone eat?

359
00:31:23,640 --> 00:31:26,000
How much do you two

360
00:31:26,800 --> 00:31:28,880
want for your trouble?

361
00:31:29,800 --> 00:31:31,560
Just say it directly.

362
00:31:31,640 --> 00:31:34,480
Let's end this and have nothing more
to do with each other.

363
00:31:40,840 --> 00:31:42,560
Don't think I can't see through you.

364
00:31:44,360 --> 00:31:48,360
Your son is nothing but a thief.

365
00:31:49,400 --> 00:31:50,240
Oh.

366
00:31:50,320 --> 00:31:51,760
Or…

367
00:31:52,280 --> 00:31:54,520
Is this your side job
after your father died?

368
00:31:54,600 --> 00:31:56,920
-Hey, Aunt--
-Wee.

369
00:31:58,720 --> 00:32:02,160
Who are you calling "aunt"?
You know you're not welcome,

370
00:32:02,240 --> 00:32:05,120
yet you're still staying?
Can you even eat?

371
00:32:05,200 --> 00:32:07,680
If it were me, I would've left long ago.

372
00:32:11,240 --> 00:32:14,920
I hope this is the last meal
we ever share.

373
00:32:15,720 --> 00:32:17,200
I hope we never meet again.

374
00:32:26,040 --> 00:32:29,720
How does someone grow up
to be this cruel, Mom?

375
00:32:31,600 --> 00:32:33,920
Maybe they lacked love growing up.

376
00:32:35,440 --> 00:32:37,080
Forget her, son.

377
00:32:37,160 --> 00:32:40,240
She must have grown up lacking love.

378
00:32:53,640 --> 00:32:55,120
I thought you had a headache.

379
00:32:56,480 --> 00:32:57,480
Uh…

380
00:32:58,040 --> 00:32:59,880
I already took medicine.

381
00:33:00,760 --> 00:33:03,840
Do you really have a headache,
or do you just not want to come down?

382
00:33:05,120 --> 00:33:06,920
They're the ones who helped me.

383
00:33:07,640 --> 00:33:10,120
Couldn't you do this for me?

384
00:33:14,640 --> 00:33:17,480
You've never acted this way before.

385
00:33:18,600 --> 00:33:19,920
Is this because of Aunt Pat?

386
00:33:23,280 --> 00:33:25,760
Aunt Pat doesn't like that mother and son.

387
00:33:26,600 --> 00:33:28,440
She told you not to go, didn't she?

388
00:33:32,560 --> 00:33:35,640
I shouldn't have left you with her.

389
00:33:36,400 --> 00:33:37,680
She's spoiled you.

390
00:33:38,840 --> 00:33:41,280
-Dad--
-Don't raise your voice at me.

391
00:33:41,360 --> 00:33:45,560
What you're doing is really bad manners.
I have to be honest with you.

392
00:33:45,640 --> 00:33:48,120
Then let me be honest too.

393
00:33:48,200 --> 00:33:52,600
I don't like her son,
and I don't want to eat with him.

394
00:34:04,680 --> 00:34:07,960
So is this what you want,
or what Alyssa wants?

395
00:34:09,199 --> 00:34:12,880
Come on, you heard her yourself.

396
00:34:12,960 --> 00:34:15,560
Alyssa doesn't like that guy.

397
00:34:15,639 --> 00:34:19,600
She's grown up now.
She's not a child anymore.

398
00:34:19,679 --> 00:34:23,920
Having dinner with a strange man
she doesn't get along with

399
00:34:24,000 --> 00:34:26,239
is hardly enjoyable.

400
00:34:26,320 --> 00:34:28,520
Who could eat?

401
00:34:39,280 --> 00:34:40,840
-Hello.
-Hello.

402
00:34:57,280 --> 00:34:59,160
Mom, I'll go talk to her.

403
00:35:00,000 --> 00:35:03,960
We need to clear things up.
Maybe she'll stop looking down on us.

404
00:35:05,760 --> 00:35:08,160
Wee! Wait, Wee!

405
00:35:18,160 --> 00:35:20,200
Oh, where did your son go?

406
00:35:21,600 --> 00:35:23,160
He followed Alyssa outside.

407
00:35:23,760 --> 00:35:26,000
He wants to explain
the misunderstanding between them.

408
00:35:26,520 --> 00:35:28,920
I'm sorry that…

409
00:35:29,000 --> 00:35:30,520
It's alright.

410
00:35:30,600 --> 00:35:32,840
I shouldn't have agreed to come.

411
00:35:33,640 --> 00:35:35,480
But I came because…

412
00:35:36,160 --> 00:35:38,200
I need your help.

413
00:35:39,920 --> 00:35:44,200
Of course. Whatever you need
help with, just tell me.

414
00:35:52,040 --> 00:35:53,920
I want to meet Ms. Nada.

415
00:35:54,800 --> 00:35:56,760
Could you help arrange a meeting with her?

416
00:36:14,640 --> 00:36:15,520
<i>Yes, boss?</i>

417
00:36:16,600 --> 00:36:20,240
Are you around here? I have a job for you.

418
00:36:20,960 --> 00:36:22,080
<i>Yes, sir.</i>

419
00:37:38,800 --> 00:37:40,680
Hey!

420
00:37:40,760 --> 00:37:42,480
-Let go of me!
-Come with me!

421
00:37:42,560 --> 00:37:44,200
-Help!
-Quiet!

422
00:37:44,280 --> 00:37:45,640
-Don't!
-Shut up!

423
00:37:46,960 --> 00:37:48,600
Hey! Let her go!

424
00:37:52,200 --> 00:37:53,800
Run!

425
00:38:08,120 --> 00:38:09,800
-I'm sorry.
-I'm sorry.

426
00:38:13,280 --> 00:38:15,840
Dad! He's been shot.

427
00:38:15,920 --> 00:38:17,320
My head…

428
00:38:18,680 --> 00:38:21,720
My head hurts so badly.
I can't take it anymore.

429
00:38:22,720 --> 00:38:23,560
Korn.

430
00:38:29,800 --> 00:38:32,160
Korn!

431
00:38:33,600 --> 00:38:37,040
-Uh, Mr. Nimit--
-Walai, Rawee's been shot.

432
00:38:46,160 --> 00:38:47,520
Wee!

433
00:38:48,680 --> 00:38:51,520
Dad, he got shot because of me.

434
00:38:51,600 --> 00:38:53,880
-It's okay, sweetheart.
-Wee!

435
00:38:53,960 --> 00:38:56,960
Wee! My son!

436
00:38:57,040 --> 00:38:58,680
Wee!

437
00:39:00,160 --> 00:39:02,040
Oh no, Wee!

438
00:39:03,440 --> 00:39:04,440
Wee!

439
00:39:05,960 --> 00:39:07,120
Wee!

440
00:39:25,880 --> 00:39:27,280
Korn!

441
00:39:28,440 --> 00:39:31,760
Korn! My son!

442
00:39:32,640 --> 00:39:35,240
Korn!

443
00:39:35,320 --> 00:39:38,640
Korn, can you hear me?

444
00:39:39,320 --> 00:39:41,760
Can you hear me? Korn!

445
00:39:45,840 --> 00:39:49,080
The patient's condition is getting worse.

446
00:39:53,840 --> 00:39:55,960
Medication will only help
relieve the pain.

447
00:39:56,040 --> 00:39:59,840
If we leave the tumor untreated,
it will continue to grow,

448
00:39:59,920 --> 00:40:02,000
and the danger will increase.

449
00:40:02,080 --> 00:40:03,920
The side effects

450
00:40:04,000 --> 00:40:06,520
could become severe,
even leading to disability or death.

451
00:40:08,400 --> 00:40:12,240
I recommend surgery as soon as possible.

452
00:40:21,760 --> 00:40:23,520
Alyssa!

453
00:40:23,600 --> 00:40:26,440
It's okay now, my dear.

454
00:40:27,360 --> 00:40:30,120
Don't be scared, Auntie's here.

455
00:40:31,760 --> 00:40:34,000
If it weren't for him helping me…

456
00:40:34,080 --> 00:40:35,920
If he hadn't come,

457
00:40:36,000 --> 00:40:39,040
-this probably wouldn't have happened.
-Please stop, Ms. Pat.

458
00:40:40,600 --> 00:40:43,280
Stop putting these negative thoughts
in my daughter's head.

459
00:40:46,880 --> 00:40:48,840
This isn't Rawee's fault at all.

460
00:40:49,360 --> 00:40:52,040
If you knew that boy might lose his future

461
00:40:52,120 --> 00:40:54,360
as a national football player
because he saved Alyssa,

462
00:40:54,440 --> 00:40:56,360
would you still say something like this?

463
00:41:05,480 --> 00:41:08,480
Go take a shower first, Alyssa.
We'll talk about this tomorrow.

464
00:41:11,880 --> 00:41:13,040
Wait, Ms. Pat.

465
00:41:18,600 --> 00:41:20,560
Take Alyssa back to Bangkok tomorrow.

466
00:41:21,560 --> 00:41:23,400
I'll take care of her withdrawal.

467
00:41:24,080 --> 00:41:26,920
I'll send her to study in America.

468
00:41:48,200 --> 00:41:51,080
Stop putting these negative thoughts
in my daughter's head.

469
00:41:51,880 --> 00:41:53,840
This isn't Rawee's fault at all.

470
00:41:54,640 --> 00:41:57,000
If you knew that boy might lose his future

471
00:41:57,080 --> 00:41:59,600
as a national football player
because he saved Alyssa,

472
00:41:59,680 --> 00:42:01,440
would you still say something like this?

473
00:42:14,720 --> 00:42:16,360
Hey! Let her go!

474
00:42:16,960 --> 00:42:18,080
Run!

475
00:42:42,880 --> 00:42:45,000
Thank you so much.

476
00:42:46,000 --> 00:42:48,960
Mr. Thamrong, how is Wee?

477
00:42:49,760 --> 00:42:50,880
The surgery went well.

478
00:42:52,400 --> 00:42:53,960
What a relief.

479
00:42:54,880 --> 00:42:55,720
But…

480
00:42:56,880 --> 00:42:58,160
But?

481
00:42:59,640 --> 00:43:01,560
He may have problems with his leg.

482
00:43:02,600 --> 00:43:05,120
We don't know how much
it will affect his football career.

483
00:43:12,120 --> 00:43:14,960
Mrs. Walai, how is Korn?

484
00:43:15,040 --> 00:43:16,880
That's not just a normal headache, is it?

485
00:43:22,480 --> 00:43:26,800
Korn has a brain tumor.
He needs surgery urgently.

486
00:43:28,560 --> 00:43:32,720
Mrs. Walai, if there's anything
Mr. Nimit and I can do to help,

487
00:43:32,800 --> 00:43:34,320
please let us know.

488
00:43:37,280 --> 00:43:38,160
Thank you.

489
00:43:40,360 --> 00:43:42,600
I'll excuse myself.

490
00:43:42,680 --> 00:43:43,760
Yes.

491
00:44:06,800 --> 00:44:07,960
Mr. Nimit.

492
00:44:08,840 --> 00:44:11,160
I've caught the person
who attacked Ms. Alyssa.

493
00:44:11,680 --> 00:44:13,240
He really is one of Mr. Jak's men.

494
00:44:14,040 --> 00:44:15,760
What would you like me to do next?

495
00:45:07,360 --> 00:45:08,280
Mom.

496
00:45:16,080 --> 00:45:19,240
Uncle Thamrong said
Korn's condition is very serious.

497
00:45:25,120 --> 00:45:27,480
Please do what I suggested.

498
00:45:28,440 --> 00:45:30,000
Tell Ms. Nada

499
00:45:30,720 --> 00:45:32,520
that Korn is her son.

500
00:45:36,840 --> 00:45:38,600
I can't do that.

501
00:45:42,400 --> 00:45:44,440
Would you let Korn risk his life

502
00:45:45,440 --> 00:45:47,360
when we have a chance to save him?

503
00:45:52,000 --> 00:45:53,480
This is the only way

504
00:45:54,360 --> 00:45:57,960
to save Korn and our family, Mom.

505
00:46:28,160 --> 00:46:29,000
Here you go.

506
00:46:30,480 --> 00:46:33,080
Good work. I knew I chose the right man.

507
00:46:55,000 --> 00:46:56,680
What have you done?

508
00:47:02,640 --> 00:47:04,640
Alyssa is your own niece.

509
00:47:06,200 --> 00:47:07,280
I didn't do it.

510
00:47:11,800 --> 00:47:15,680
With this much evidence against you,
you still dare to deny it?

511
00:47:20,680 --> 00:47:23,160
Alyssa is my only daughter.

512
00:47:23,760 --> 00:47:25,320
What I give my daughter

513
00:47:25,400 --> 00:47:29,280
is up to me.
It has nothing to do with you.

514
00:47:30,360 --> 00:47:32,280
I don't have to give you anything.

515
00:47:36,120 --> 00:47:37,480
Don't forget,

516
00:47:38,400 --> 00:47:40,640
we split the inheritance equally.

517
00:47:43,240 --> 00:47:46,600
You've already wasted your share.

518
00:47:47,640 --> 00:47:49,520
Now you're trying to take
your niece's too?

519
00:47:50,200 --> 00:47:53,240
-Isn't that a bit shameless?
-What do you want from me? Just say it.

520
00:47:53,920 --> 00:47:56,040
You control my life anyway.

521
00:48:00,080 --> 00:48:01,760
You'll run the resort on Tawan Island.

522
00:48:06,520 --> 00:48:08,480
I'm removing you from the factory.

523
00:48:08,560 --> 00:48:11,600
-Isn't that going too far?
-You have no right to demand anything.

524
00:48:12,120 --> 00:48:16,080
What you need to do is prove yourself.

525
00:48:16,160 --> 00:48:20,160
Prove that there's more to you
than your rotten nature.

526
00:48:21,480 --> 00:48:23,680
If I give you the resort now,

527
00:48:25,120 --> 00:48:26,560
you'll just sell it all.

528
00:48:30,080 --> 00:48:34,040
From now on, don't ever do
anything this vile again.

529
00:48:35,360 --> 00:48:37,640
This is your last chance.

530
00:48:44,960 --> 00:48:46,040
Remember this.

531
00:48:48,080 --> 00:48:51,520
Between my brother and my daughter,
I choose my daughter.

532
00:49:08,920 --> 00:49:10,320
Alyssa.

533
00:49:10,960 --> 00:49:15,200
Are you ready? We should get going.
We'll arrive in Bangkok late.

534
00:49:18,200 --> 00:49:19,400
Alyssa.

535
00:49:26,680 --> 00:49:31,680
Alyssa, my dear. Alyssa!

536
00:49:33,880 --> 00:49:35,080
Where did she go?

537
00:49:48,840 --> 00:49:52,000
<i>Mom, the club's football player is here!</i>

538
00:49:52,080 --> 00:49:54,840
-Great job, son. My son is the best.
-Thank you.

539
00:50:05,160 --> 00:50:09,040
RAWEE WITTAYADUMRONG - PLAYER

540
00:50:22,160 --> 00:50:25,680
-Hello, Mr. Nimit.
-I've arranged a meeting with Ms. Nada.

541
00:50:27,480 --> 00:50:28,520
Thank you.

542
00:50:29,400 --> 00:50:31,080
<i>Are you available at 2 p.m. today?</i>

543
00:50:31,720 --> 00:50:33,480
Yes, I am.

544
00:50:34,080 --> 00:50:35,600
Then let's meet at the factory.

545
00:50:36,800 --> 00:50:39,840
Okay. Thank you so much, Mr. Nimit.

546
00:50:41,840 --> 00:50:43,160
MON 1 JUN

547
00:50:59,200 --> 00:51:03,680
LOVE, RAWEE
NADA TAYAWAT

548
00:51:19,520 --> 00:51:21,160
Can you remember anything?

549
00:51:26,760 --> 00:51:27,760
Yes.

550
00:51:29,760 --> 00:51:31,680
This is definitely my handwriting.

551
00:51:45,840 --> 00:51:47,440
Do you remember this ring?

552
00:51:50,440 --> 00:51:54,400
I found it in the baby's belongings,
so I kept it safe.

553
00:51:59,440 --> 00:52:03,680
I thought this ring could help prove
the child's identity

554
00:52:03,760 --> 00:52:05,600
and show that he is your son.

555
00:52:16,200 --> 00:52:17,200
My father

556
00:52:17,960 --> 00:52:20,880
made this ring for all his children.

557
00:52:27,280 --> 00:52:31,240
Could you tell me in detail
what happened back then?

558
00:52:35,960 --> 00:52:37,240
Of course.

559
00:52:51,680 --> 00:52:53,160
What's up, Wee?

560
00:52:57,600 --> 00:52:59,600
There's something important
you need to know.

561
00:53:04,040 --> 00:53:05,480
Ms. Nada Tayawat

562
00:53:06,760 --> 00:53:08,200
is my mother.

563
00:53:11,080 --> 00:53:12,160
Wait.

564
00:53:12,240 --> 00:53:16,080
Dad and Mom said you were Aunt's son.

565
00:53:18,640 --> 00:53:22,640
They had to lie to protect me.

566
00:53:23,920 --> 00:53:25,000
Wow.

567
00:53:25,080 --> 00:53:26,480
Tayawat?

568
00:53:27,200 --> 00:53:31,120
That's a rich family's surname.
Are you a rich kid, Wee?

569
00:53:31,800 --> 00:53:33,800
You don't have to worry
about the club anymore.

570
00:53:33,880 --> 00:53:36,040
You're rich now, so don't forget me.

571
00:53:36,960 --> 00:53:39,080
We have to switch places, Korn.

572
00:53:45,200 --> 00:53:49,080
What do you mean, Wee?
Is this really the time to joke?

573
00:53:50,360 --> 00:53:51,720
I'm not joking.

574
00:53:54,080 --> 00:53:55,880
Mom and I already talked about this.

575
00:53:56,960 --> 00:53:59,840
We have to find a way to get you treated.

576
00:54:00,920 --> 00:54:02,800
This is the best solution.

577
00:54:05,680 --> 00:54:07,360
You're her son.

578
00:54:07,440 --> 00:54:10,480
You could just ask her
to help me get treatment.

579
00:54:10,560 --> 00:54:12,320
But if you're not her son,

580
00:54:13,240 --> 00:54:15,480
she might not help us.

581
00:54:16,960 --> 00:54:18,560
Once you're better,

582
00:54:19,600 --> 00:54:21,840
we can tell her the truth.

583
00:54:23,840 --> 00:54:25,800
But if your surgery doesn't work,

584
00:54:27,280 --> 00:54:29,920
she'll be able to take care of you
for the rest of your life.

585
00:54:34,520 --> 00:54:36,040
I love you so much, Korn.

586
00:54:38,440 --> 00:54:40,880
I'd do anything for my little brother.

587
00:54:48,480 --> 00:54:51,000
We'll always take care of each other
until the day we die.

588
00:55:05,800 --> 00:55:07,640
Why has no one in my family

589
00:55:08,640 --> 00:55:10,880
ever mentioned this before?

590
00:55:13,000 --> 00:55:15,440
They probably thought
the child had died, like I did.

591
00:55:15,520 --> 00:55:18,480
So no one wanted to bring it up
and upset you.

592
00:55:23,360 --> 00:55:25,600
Thank you, Mrs. Walai,

593
00:55:25,680 --> 00:55:28,720
for taking such good care of my son.

594
00:55:36,320 --> 00:55:39,320
Da, I think you should take a DNA test.

595
00:55:42,760 --> 00:55:45,520
No. I won't take one.

596
00:55:46,720 --> 00:55:48,640
I remember everything now.

597
00:55:49,320 --> 00:55:51,360
The evidence is already so clear.

598
00:55:51,960 --> 00:55:56,560
If I make him take a DNA test,
how hurt would he be?

599
00:55:59,480 --> 00:56:02,400
His mother abandoned him
and never raised him,

600
00:56:02,480 --> 00:56:06,120
and now she still doesn't believe
he's her own son.

601
00:56:07,520 --> 00:56:11,920
If I were him, I would never accept that.

602
00:56:14,520 --> 00:56:17,600
I'm just worried your relatives

603
00:56:17,680 --> 00:56:19,320
won't accept him as part of the family.

604
00:56:20,040 --> 00:56:23,600
I don't care who refuses to accept him.
He's my son, and that's enough.

605
00:56:27,560 --> 00:56:28,400
Mrs. Walai.

606
00:56:30,560 --> 00:56:33,840
Could you take me to see my son now?

607
00:56:33,920 --> 00:56:35,840
Oh. Yes, of course.

608
00:56:38,840 --> 00:56:40,040
Walai.

609
00:56:40,840 --> 00:56:44,640
Is he your eldest son
or your youngest son?

610
00:57:34,960 --> 00:57:37,760
I promise I'll do everything I can
to bring our family

611
00:57:37,840 --> 00:57:40,120
<i>back to the way it was when Dad was here.</i>

612
00:57:41,560 --> 00:57:43,280
<i>If this hadn't happened,</i>

613
00:57:43,840 --> 00:57:47,400
someone like you would never have wanted
anything to do with me.

614
00:57:48,880 --> 00:57:50,840
<i>I have something to announce to everyone.</i>

615
00:57:50,920 --> 00:57:53,640
I'm sending Phakorn to study in America.

616
00:57:55,040 --> 00:57:56,680
Don't be afraid of the pain, Korn.

617
00:57:57,600 --> 00:58:01,280
You won't feel anything.
Just sleep for a while, and it'll be over.

618
00:58:03,680 --> 00:58:05,640
<i>Aren't you going to say goodbye to them?</i>

619
00:58:06,160 --> 00:58:08,200
I don't want to show weakness
in front of others.

620
00:58:08,920 --> 00:58:10,760
<i>I'd rather look ahead.</i>

621
00:58:11,760 --> 00:58:15,040
You found your son,
but won't bring him to meet your family?

622
00:58:15,120 --> 00:58:17,680
Because I'm afraid my son

623
00:58:17,760 --> 00:58:20,120
will meet the same fate as his father.

624
00:59:01,720 --> 00:59:04,840
Subtitle translation by:
Chomchanach Yanaharn
